,"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T17:35:01-07:00","id":1554704,"title":"","content":"Through the Technocracy the SI might succeed, that would be an interesting scenario but very definitive.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T17:40:02-07:00","id":1554705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554704#post1554704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through the Technocracy the SI might succeed, that would be an interesting scenario but very definitive.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I agree that in a united world of darkness, the SI's success is probably because it's being bankrolled by the Union and the only reason the SI HAVEN'T revealed vampires to the public is because the Union is making that support conditional on secrecy.<br /> <br /> The SI is just their proxy for dealing with the undead so they don't have to get their hands too dirty but the Union is supplying them like the CIA does guerillas. Others may want to keep the Technocracy out of their VTM games.<br /> <br /> It resolves a lot of unanswered questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T18:39:38-07:00","id":1554707,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think 2 is the most likely.<br /> <br /> At some point the SI just gets so big and has so many players and the actions it's taking are so extraordinary that it's inevitable that people will begin talking, showing videos, etc., the truth is going to get out. It's already kind of hard to believe that the SI is dropping massive bombs on NATO countries without any major leaks. Plus, on top of that, if many Kindred decide that the Masquerade no longer protects them, then eventually you'll have large numbers of Kindred decide that there's little reason to continue to maintain it and that the best chance for survival is to get as many humans on their side as possible (offering immortality and things like that).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T21:43:57-07:00","id":1554712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554705#post1554705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Personally, I agree that in a united world of darkness, the SI's success is probably because it's being bankrolled by the Union and the only reason the SI HAVEN'T revealed vampires to the public is because the Union is making that support conditional on secrecy.<br /> <br /> The SI is just their proxy for dealing with the undead so they don't have to get their hands too dirty but the Union is supplying them like the CIA does guerillas. Others may want to keep the Technocracy out of their VTM games.<br /> <br /> It resolves a lot of unanswered questions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense.<br /> <br /> If vampires are revealed to the world, the world will then ask &quot;so vampires exist, what more does?&quot; and that goes against Technocracy intentions.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T22:18:31-07:00","id":1554715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554704#post1554704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Through the Technocracy the SI might succeed, that would be an interesting scenario but very definitive.<br /> <br /> - Saga</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it would be very definitive, and in general it means more &quot;the Union wins&quot; than &quot;the SI wins&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nothing is too definitive because completely wiping out something is far, far harder than just winning over it. Vampires have too many ways to drop out of sight individually for this to be feasible even for the Technocracy. And it is even harder for an institution that's baked by them, but don't have actual Enlightened personnel of their own.<br /> <br /> All scenarios are very interesting on their own, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> here, 2 is just the most probable, hands down. In fact, it's likely regardless of the SI, but it makes the Masquerade even less tenable. I personally think V5 should have dropped the Global Masquerade from the beginning as a starting point for the game.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is untenable. It is by itself one of the most contrived elements of the game since ever, and time only makes it harder to keep. Small-scale Masquerades are easier to do, hiding from the local masses that <i>the local vampires</i> exist, or at least some of them. But humanity as a whole probably would learn that vampires in general exist sooner rather than later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T22:27:27-07:00","id":1554716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554715#post1554715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it would be very definitive, and in general it means more &quot;the Union wins&quot; than &quot;the SI wins&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nothing is too definitive because completely wiping out something is far, far harder than just winning over it. Vampires have too many ways to drop out of sight individually for this to be feasible even for the Technocracy. And it is even harder for an institution that's baked by them, but don't have actual Enlightened personnel of their own.<br /> <br /> All scenarios are very interesting on their own, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> here, 2 is just the most probable, hands down. In fact, it's likely regardless of the SI, but it makes the Masquerade even less tenable. I personally think V5 should have dropped the Global Masquerade from the beginning as a starting point for the game.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is untenable. It is by itself one of the most contrived elements of the game since ever, and time only makes it harder to keep. Small-scale Masquerades are easier to do, hiding from the local masses that <i>the local vampires</i> exist, or at least some of them. But humanity as a whole probably would learn that vampires in general exist sooner rather than later.</div> </div> </div> </div>It'd be an interesting premise but not really THE MASQUERADE anymore.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the past few years have told me plenty of people will believe anything. The nature of the lie isn't that some people won't believe in vampires, it's that they won't believe what vampires are and will not believe vampires around them.<br /> <br /> In any case, thanks for reading my essay!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-27T22:40:01-07:00","id":1554718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554716#post1554716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It'd be an interesting premise but not really THE MASQUERADE anymore.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the past few years have told me plenty of people will believe anything. The nature of the lie isn't that some people won't believe in vampires, it's that they won't believe what vampires are and will not believe vampires around them.<br /> <br /> In any case, thanks for reading my essay!</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 isn't the Masquerade anymore in many ways. A big part of its problem with many people is that it is a not-Masquerade game that shies off from being not-Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition itself is one of the more not-Masquerade elements. VtM has never been about the looming threat of a global-spanning conspiracy to hunt vampires that at best subtly affects how vampire society has to organize and how much access it has to technology, and at worst keeps everyone permanently under high alert because there are heat-detecting cameras all over the city.<br /> <br /> What V5 frequently makes is to just pretend its own added elements don't exist so you can play Masquerade despite the setting, not following it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T05:01:20-07:00","id":1554719,"title":"","content":"Personally, I quite like 6, particularly the inexplicable version.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T06:27:08-07:00","id":1554724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554719#post1554719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I quite like 6, particularly the inexplicable version.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just remembered of the <i>Encephalitis Lethargica</i> pandemic of 1915, that inspired the first story of Neil Gaiman's <i>Sandman</i>. More than 1 million people around the world developing a sudden sleep disorder with brutal effects and no discernible source, that never got explained. There's even a 1990 movie about it with Robin Willians and Robert De Niro, <i>Awakenings</i>.<br /> <br /> Today it's thought that at least 8 epidemics of the disease happened in the last 500 years, which suggests it may come back any day, without warning, and we still know next to nothing about it. And it would be a very interesting thing to happen to the SI in this scenario, with either subtle or overt supernatural cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T07:50:51-07:00","id":1554725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I just remembered of the <i>Encephalitis Lethargica</i> pandemic of 1915, that inspired the first story of Neil Gaiman's <i>Sandman</i>. More than 1 million people around the world developing a sudden sleep disorder with brutal effects and no discernible source, that never got explained. There's even a 1990 movie about it with Robin Willians and Robert De Niro, <i>Awakenings</i>.<br /> <br /> Today it's thought that at least 8 epidemics of the disease happened in the last 500 years, which suggests it may come back any day, without warning, and we still know next to nothing about it. And it would be a very interesting thing to happen to the SI in this scenario, with either subtle or overt supernatural cause. </div> </div> </div>For me, I was actually thinking of the Arabian Nights-esque kingdom that disappeared from the same series. The Second Inquisition are poking creatures that might someday simply make them into nothing more than a dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-29-2025, 12:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T07:51:27-07:00","id":1554726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554715#post1554715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think it would be very definitive, and in general it means more &quot;the Union wins&quot; than &quot;the SI wins&quot;.<br /> <br /> Nothing is too definitive because completely wiping out something is far, far harder than just winning over it. Vampires have too many ways to drop out of sight individually for this to be feasible even for the Technocracy. And it is even harder for an institution that's baked by them, but don't have actual Enlightened personnel of their own.<br /> <br /> All scenarios are very interesting on their own, but I'm with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> here, 2 is just the most probable, hands down. In fact, it's likely regardless of the SI, but it makes the Masquerade even less tenable. I personally think V5 should have dropped the Global Masquerade from the beginning as a starting point for the game.<br /> <br /> The Masquerade is untenable. It is by itself one of the most contrived elements of the game since ever, and time only makes it harder to keep. Small-scale Masquerades are easier to do, hiding from the local masses that <i>the local vampires</i> exist, or at least some of them. But humanity as a whole probably would learn that vampires in general exist sooner rather than later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know much about Mage specially after the deah of Ravnos on how much did it cost to the Technocracy to kill him. If it's a duable thing again, then yeah, there is a probable &quot;Union wins&quot; scenario. Now, if it was a one thing, that's problematic because there are at least 12 more to go and now they know they have an common enemy that can wipe them. I'd go with the 3rd scenario. The second one is the one thing the SI don't want and they mught have made the logisticts on how humans would react to the existence of vampires.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T07:51:50-07:00","id":1554727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554718#post1554718\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> V5 isn't the Masquerade anymore in many ways. A big part of its problem with many people is that it is a not-Masquerade game that shies off from being not-Masquerade.<br /> <br /> The Second Inquisition itself is one of the more not-Masquerade elements. VtM has never been about the looming threat of a global-spanning conspiracy to hunt vampires that at best subtly affects how vampire society has to organize and how much access it has to technology, and at worst keeps everyone permanently under high alert because there are heat-detecting cameras all over the city.<br /> <br /> What V5 frequently makes is to just pretend its own added elements don't exist so you can play Masquerade despite the setting, not following it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings up what I had a problem with THE SECOND INQUISITION book and why I realized that I'd been reading the writer's intentions all along. Basically, for a lot of fans, the Second Inquisition was this massive police state organization that would be able to track down and systematically eliminate vampires across the globe via anonymous military strikes during the day and burning the buildings down around them. It's a horrifying situation that means that vampire society has to cease to exist.<br /> <br /> It's not that.<br /> <br /> Instead, the intention seemed to be Blade-ifying the games more. Basically, heavily armed guys in a scary gas masks charging at the vampires in the middle of the night and getting into big fights where the vampires tear them apart with disciplines. They're basically a replacement for the Sabbat as disposable mooks and also primarily meant to be enemies in the video games.<br /> <br /> This is related to the Sabbat in that I believe the changes done to them aren't necessarily for the tabletop game but to establish them as disposable mooks for future video games. The SI and Sabbat existing less as characters to play and more for providing enemies in lore. It happened in Swansong as huge chunks of the game is killing SI soldiers like Selene or Bloodrayne. Now in Bloodlines 2, you get to slaughter whole swaths of Hunters and Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Maybe I'm right or maybe I'm wrong but the assumption is that the Hunters are there to provide the game orcs or goblins.<br /> <br /> It's not a bad thing, games need antagonists, but in the SI book you have less discussion of the politics behind the SI and more talk about light grenades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T09:12:54-07:00","id":1554729,"title":"","content":"Very nice and well tought out scenarios<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end#post1554700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[<br /> <br /> <b>2:] Broken Masquerade (Neutral): </b>The Second Inquisition makes a calculated decision that the only way to maintain their momentum against the blank body scourge is to come clean. The Masquerade is broken repeatedly and in such a way as to be undeniable. The leaders think that humanity will unite and destroy the undead menace. Unfortunately, for the Inquisition, they have forgotten that mankind cannot collectively agree water is wet.<br /> <br /> Some react with hatred, horror, and a desire to eradicate the undead. Others, however, believe them to be victims of a terrible disease or people who can be coexisted with. Others still don't care about the morality of it and see only a cure for death, illness, and the mundanity of their lives. The world is re-arranged among vampire kingdoms, vampire war zones, and places with elaborate sets of laws to deal with the undead. Other supernaturals may struggle with the fact they are also outed but do not wish to be lumped with humanity's predators. The Second Inquisition loses its greatest weapon during this time: unaccountability.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>But I would call this a <b>Kindred Victory</b> and a hard one instead of neutral outcome<br /> Arguably Dracula basically laid the ground work for this and while Dracula in Bram Stoker's novel is not a romantic hero; he is a monstrous villain driven by bloodlust and conquest, the popular image of a romantic, brooding Dracula, the creation of later adaptations, especially films, that added love stories and romantic elements to the character firmly hardwired in the collective &quot;hive mind&quot; of Humanity<br /> In the 21st century even in WoD (thanks to the Masquarade) you can't really find a place where people are <i>actually</i> fear or hate vampires - well maybe Serbia and Southeast Asia (vampire-like spirits persist in countries like Malaysia, Thailand, and the Philippines. In modern times, these beliefs have combined with contemporary anxieties, with rumors of &quot;organ harvesters&quot; often echoing traditional vampire fears of unseen predators preying on people). Maybe Ghana with the asanbosam, but we are really would scrap the bottom of the barrel with that one<br /> If the SI would shatter the Masquarade and they would come clean: &quot;look, vampires exist and probably you even knew a few just never realized&quot; most of humanity porbably just shurg or would say &quot;cool&quot;<br /> What remained of the Sabbat maybe would show the &quot;ugly face&quot; of Vampires (tho' the frightening tought humanity would say the Sabbat &quot;okay but they are at leats not [insert whatever here] ) but the Cainite probably would ride what humanity managed to twist the original myths/racial memory - eg. what evolved from the traditional monster: an alluring, complex character, often with a Byronic hero-like quality. Lestat, Edward, Camilla, any Dracula basically, whataver the late 20th century produced as &quot; Vampire \u200b&quot;... Humans probably would spread their arms and welcome the undead &quot;monsters&quot;<br /> It would be like a bit when Loki ran for President in Marvel<br /> \u200b\u200bAs you wrote, the world would re-arrange itself in to blood kingdoms, especially if a few local hero, mythycal figure or outright God would crawl out from their ancient tombs<br /> Just immagine if Sobek, the legendary Mokol\u00e9 Abomination, Embraced through rituals by Sutekh himself in the 4th Generation slumbering in a Founding Temple of Faiyum, the Crocodile Temple would awake and would come forth all in his terrible albino reptilian glory... <br /> But you don't have to go that far back, just immagine a vampire who would come forth, I am over 300 years old, I was Embraced here in America, and I love my Country I fought in the Civil War on the side of the Union and maybe helped to win a few close calls with the Gifts of Caine... and since then I am protecting in every night; I lived and died for my country and my dead heart still beats for it ! - he would ends up President in no time...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T10:29:32-07:00","id":1554730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554729#post1554729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just immagine if Sobek, the legendary Mokol\u00e9 Abomination, Embraced through rituals by Sutekh himself in the 4th Generation slumbering in a Founding Temple of Faiyum, the Crocodile Temple would awake and would come forth all in his terrible albino reptilian glory...</div> </div> </div> </div>I would imagine that the Nagah would kill him in short order, given that slaying corrupt Khurah who have evaded their own kind's justice is their thing. And with Lance of the Summer Sun, there wouldn't be anything left.<br /> <br /> (Snakes can fire sunbeam lasers at targets. Against Followers of Set, it's super effective!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T10:42:30-07:00","id":1554731,"title":"","content":"Personally i think the masquarade would become more robust than less, with the increasing sense of unreality irl The moment the vampires start resuming a proactive approach to masquarade enforcement its all over. With that in mind 8 seems likely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T15:03:01-07:00","id":1554745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saga</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554726#post1554726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know much about Mage specially after the deah of Ravnos on how much did it cost to the Technocracy to kill him. If it's a duable thing again, then yeah, there is a probable &quot;Union wins&quot; scenario. Now, if it was a one thing, that's problematic because there are at least 12 more to go and now they know they have an common enemy that can wipe them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was mostly a one-off, the three magical nukes they used were almost all they had. They actually had a fourth one, but that one <i>also</i> got used. In the Labyrinth, kicking off the 6th Maelstrom and possibly the Avatar Storm.<br /> <br /> But that said, being funded by the Union wouldn't be enough to give the SI a victory if they can't do it by themselves, and when the Union enters the game directly it changes a lot, too much to call it the SI anymore, as we're talking supernatural resources.<br /> <br /> And I don't think blowing up the Antes is relevant. Vampire society is a different beast altogether, defeating one doesn't entails defeating the other, they require very distinct tools altogether.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554729#post1554729\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I would call this a <b>Kindred Victory</b> and a hard one instead of neutral outcome</div> </div> </div> </div>While I mostly agree with the conclusion, there's a lot of oversimplifications and assumptions here.<br /> <br /> Legends about vampire-like entities aren't that important. The rest of the world is no more of a superstition-laden place than the US. Most people everywhere know what an Anne Rice vampire is (even when they don't know by her name). The tangent about local legends was racist.<br /> <br /> That said, there's a world of difference between liking something in a piece of fiction and liking it for real, as many LGBTQIAP+ people can tell you from their experiences coming out for progressive parents and friends. And a lot more doubts about what's really going on here.<br /> <br /> Overall people would be more open than the SI wants/expects, but how this unfolds would depend a lot on what both sides do and say, and their PR. Overall the SI has far weaker PR than the Camarilla, so there's that as far as we can say.<br /> <br /> A lot of things will vary, though, there would be no consensus for a long, long time. And again, as any minority or foreigner can tell you, you don't need a lot of bigots for them to make your life very bad and very hard. Being openly a vampire would be doable, but would be dangerous nonetheless and far from guaranteed you'd have nice neighbors.<br /> <br /> Sobek would probably be angry and eat some people. He's from a time when there was no Masquerade, from a place where two powerful vampire <i>armies</i> ruled openly, and he slept this whole time. How much the world accepts him at first makes no difference, he'd screw things up royally being him.\u200b<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554730#post1554730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the Nagah would kill him in short order</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they wouldn't. Don't be silly, Nagah aren't real.<br /> <br /> It's just that if no one else killed him on site, he would disappear without notice in a few days. Any witness would be able to testify that he simply burst into flames, as his kind should by the way, as if hit by the sun despite being indoors at night.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T15:43:01-07:00","id":1554747,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy is an interesting storyline to view with the metaplot as they become increasingly impotent the less evil they become. In 2nd Edition, they were an all powerful conspiracy that ruled most of the world but due to Revised making them no longer full-on baddies (regardless of what horrible evil shit they were doing in the NWO Revised book's opening), they've lost 90% of their influence and members so they're more like the Traditions now in that they're rebelling against society versus dominating it.<br /> <br /> The SAD was probably the richest of the Syndicate for example and they've defected to become full-on Nephandus for example while the rest became Threat Null.<br /> <br /> So, while they certainly can HELP the SI, I'd argue that in a shared WOD universe, the Technocracy is funding the SI as a proxy organization (and ignoring the Society of Leopold's extensive Celestial Choir-backed influence [or Knights Templar]) because they can't do the kind of military operations they used to.<br /> <br /> As I pointed out in one of my games, though, a bunch of the SI being clones like Victors or MIB would explain how they can apparently send hordes of disposable troops and no one in the US government noticing the 300 or so losses on US soil. Which is a lot even for America.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-28T22:00:11-07:00","id":1554756,"title":"","content":"That's quite an oversimplification of how the Union changed.<br /> <br /> Nowhere was it ever denied their crimes to begin with. Guide to the Technocracy (a 2nd Ed supplement) makes it perfectly clear that a game of Union agents is a lot about trying to fix it from the inside, because its crimes are real and are many. Also, the idea that the Technocracy isn't in full control of things (even so we can have other enemies be a danger, like the Nefandi) is old news in 2nd Ed.<br /> <br /> But what weakened the Technocracy was specifically the Avatar Storm, the same thing that weakened the Traditions. They just had more to lose. The notion of corruption within is also a recognition of the place of both the Nefandi in the game and the Wyrm in the Metaplot.<br /> <br /> Anyway, backing up from the Union can help in a number of ways, but not everything. It's a matter of theme and mood: if you give the SI overtly Technocratic resources, they become a very different thing to deal with. It stops being about the enemy we read about in Vampire and starts to be about a crossover with this whole new splat with a lot of elements and themes that may be great at a game of &quot;Vampire With a Twist&quot;, but just doesn't mesh well with standard Vampire.<br /> <br /> It isn't bad <i>per se</i>. I just wouldn't classify it <i>narratively </i>as the SI, even if they identify as such in the fiction. I'd classify it as another option, where another splat comes and sets it all down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T13:29:16-07:00","id":1554790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554745#post1554745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they wouldn't. Don't be silly, Nagah aren't real.<br /> <br /> It's just that if no one else killed him on site, he would disappear without notice in a few days. Any witness would be able to testify that he simply burst into flames, as his kind should by the way, as if hit by the sun despite being indoors at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, of course.<br /> <br /> (And the hypothetical W:tA metaplot would have the decency not to mention the name or names of any particular killers so the PCs could step into that role.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:18:27-07:00","id":1554814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554756#post1554756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's quite an oversimplification of how the Union changed.<br /> <br /> Nowhere was it ever denied their crimes to begin with. Guide to the Technocracy (a 2nd Ed supplement) makes it perfectly clear that a game of Union agents is a lot about trying to fix it from the inside, because its crimes are real and are many. Also, the idea that the Technocracy isn't in full control of things (even so we can have other enemies be a danger, like the Nefandi) is old news in 2nd Ed.<br /> <br /> But what weakened the Technocracy was specifically the Avatar Storm, the same thing that weakened the Traditions. They just had more to lose. The notion of corruption within is also a recognition of the place of both the Nefandi in the game and the Wyrm in the Metaplot.<br /> <br /> Anyway, backing up from the Union can help in a number of ways, but not everything. It's a matter of theme and mood: if you give the SI overtly Technocratic resources, they become a very different thing to deal with. It stops being about the enemy we read about in Vampire and starts to be about a crossover with this whole new splat with a lot of elements and themes that may be great at a game of &quot;Vampire With a Twist&quot;, but just doesn't mesh well with standard Vampire.<br /> <br /> It isn't bad <i>per se</i>. I just wouldn't classify it <i>narratively </i>as the SI, even if they identify as such in the fiction. I'd classify it as another option, where another splat comes and sets it all down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think whether or not incorporating the Technocracy works for your game or not is something that depends on how you like to incorporate conspiracy into your games. I was a huge fan of PROJECT: TWILIGHT (a Werewolf supplement) and part of that book's premise was the US government was controlled by agents of the Camarilla, Technocracy, and Pentex all tripping over one another while not realizing they were doing it. Humorously, the Sabbat had numerous high profile agents in the NSA who didn't use any of their resources properly because they didn't have any respect for human technology.<br /> <br /> If I were to use the Technocracy in a Second Inquisition game, I wouldn't use it as a case of introducing massive super tech and so on but as a bunch of hints that the SI are getting resources that they shouldn't have and shouldn't exist. Things like large scale hidden military bases, advanced technology (but not sci-fi, more improbably Tom Clancy with a vampire strain), and a lot of soldiers that someone should be missing. Enough that the Kindred can suspect it might be someone like the Tremere or Ventrue or Endron behind it.<br /> <br /> Mind you, the difference in scales should be leveled to an extent as well. Without the Umbra, the Technocracy is far more on the level that can be opposed by vampires. It's still suicide to go head first on them (a Hit Mark V is a amazing killing machine to vampires) but enough that they could car bomb the local Comptroller without any coincidences protecting him because that's not how the Union works.<br /> <br /> And this being Vampire, the most cynical ending might be the best one where the Technocracy and Camarilla make a formal treaty about the Masquerade and the SI loses its benefactor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T20:46:36-07:00","id":1554817,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554725#post1554725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I was actually thinking of the Arabian Nights-esque kingdom that disappeared from the same series. The Second Inquisition are poking creatures that might someday simply make them into nothing more than a dream.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irem of the Pillars, the very same Irem used in <i>Mummy: the Curse</i>. It's an actual legend, some kind of Desert Atlantis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554700-essay-how-the-second-inquisition-will-end?p=1554814#post1554814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think whether or not incorporating the Technocracy works for your game or not is something that depends on how you like to incorporate conspiracy into your games.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's where I point to the version where the Union just &quot;funds&quot; them.<br /> <br /> The SI is already Conspiracy a lot, as actually is everything in Vampire. The Union itself may flavor the conspiracy, but you can adjust the Illuminati level of the chronicle a lot without really changing if it is the SI or not.<br /> <br /> Giving Union funding to them makes for a good conspiracy plot, but then you can do it with a lot of other conspirators without significantly changing things. It could be the Union. It could be a spirit or a Werewolf group (especially if you stay closer to W20 lore on them instead of W5, so you can use rich kinfolk conspirators). It could be Endron.<br /> <br /> Being the Union only really matters when you add Union-specific resources, and then the game changes. It isn't necessarily easier or harder, but it is meaningfully different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:03:32-07:00","id":1554819,"title":"","content":"I think Irem was also the basis for the third Uncharted Game. <br /> <br /> I also used it as the basis for a short story in Tales of the Al-Azif where Abdul Al-Hazred first learns of the Great Old Ones from the Yithians living there in stolen bodies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:24:17-07:00","id":1554824,"title":"","content":"Yes, it was the basis of Uncharted 3. Although I must admit I never played any game of the series.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft and his clique wrote a lot of stories using or mentioning Irem, they kind of popularized this spelling instead of Iram.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-29T21:28:39-07:00","id":1554825,"title":"","content":"In any case, I do think the Second Inquisition winding down instead of winding up works better for the long term health of the setting. I will also give credit that the game has managed to finangle a lot of plots out of the game.<br /> <br /> Swansong and Fall of London were probably the best uses of the SI.<br /> <br /> Swansong because the entire plot of the game is figuring out how to destroy a local branch and showing the cracks starting to form. You also get a sense why they're not the good guys even when faced with vampires given their lack of care for collateral damage.<br /> <br /> Fall of London because it took the Vienna theory and had Mithras do it for London. It's a lot easier to believe they could beat the Kindred of London when it's a Methuselah being MASSIVELY petty to his former followers.<br /> <br /> But if I had to give my favorite use, it was probably &quot;Flyboy&quot; of Chicago by Night as just the idea of a Thin Blood being used as a mole offered so many possibilities while also making it clear that once he tasted the immense power of being a Kindred, he'd want more not less.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't think of it as a permanent setting feature.<br /> <br /> Something must go.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}